Theorem RL-24: bidirectional matching of logical owner-credit/release pairs

  Preconditions:
    - A candidate owner-credit and release refer to the same logical identity.
    - Forward and backward dataflow facts are available across blocks.

  Soundness property:
    A pair is matched iff both directions identify the same credit discharge.
    This is a logical event relation; physical counter instructions and their
    placement are projection details.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate both, forward-only, backward-only, and neither directions.
    Coverage gate: 4 cases; only the both-directions case matches.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl24_bidirectional_pair_matching)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-24 matches logical owner-credit/release pairs only when both dataflow directions agree
